---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Swimming Pool"
  description="The Dartington community swimming pool — built by volunteers in 1975, closed since 2022, and now fundraising £1,093,000 to reopen."
  ogImage="/images/facilities/pool-og.jpg"
  bodyClass="zone-pool"
>

  <section class="mw-zone-hero">
    <div class="mw-wrap">
      <span class="mw-eyebrow">Community facility</span>
      <h1>Swimming Pool</h1>
      <p>Built by the community in 1975. Being rebuilt by it again.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LATEST UPDATE -->
  <section class="mw-sect">
    <div class="mw-wrap">
      <div class="pool-update">
        <div class="pool-update-main">
          <span class="mw-eyebrow">Latest update &middot; October 2026</span>
          <h2>Our pool has a plan. Now let&rsquo;s build it.</h2>
          <p class="pool-lead">We now have a detailed, professionally costed plan for the new pool and a five-year business plan showing how it can run sustainably. That moves us into a new phase: raising the money to build it.</p>
          <div class="pool-target">
            <span class="pool-target-label">Our fundraising target</span>
            <span class="pool-target-figure">&pound;1,093,000</span>
            <span class="pool-target-sub">to bring Dartington&rsquo;s community pool back</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pool-update-actions">
            <a href="/donate?campaign=pool" class="mw-btn mw-btn-primary">Donate to the pool</a>
            <a href="/contact" class="mw-btn mw-btn-secondary">Offer your help</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-status">
          <h3>Where we are</h3>
          <ul>
            <li class="done"><strong>Planning permission granted</strong> February 2025, with support from 334 people and no objections</li>
            <li class="done"><strong>Solar panels installed</strong> 80 panels and battery storage on the pavilion roof, ready to heat the pool</li>
            <li class="done"><strong>Costs estimated</strong> by independent construction cost consultants</li>
            <li class="done"><strong>Business plan complete</strong> a five-year plan for running the pool sustainably</li>
            <li class="now"><strong>Fundraising underway</strong> we have raised money already and are continuing to raise more through grants, trusts, developer contributions and community support</li>
            <li class="next"><strong>Aiming to reopen in 2028</strong></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <details class="pool-detail">
        <summary>The detail behind the numbers</summary>
        <div class="pool-detail-body">
          <p><strong>&pound;1,093,000 is the independent cost estimate for the pool.</strong> It comes from our five-year business plan and covers the full build plus professional fees, a risk allowance, inflation up to opening and VAT. Some costs can&rsquo;t be known until the project goes out to tender and building starts, so we will keep this page updated as the numbers firm up.</p>
          <p><strong>This target is for Phase 1: the pool itself.</strong> That covers extending it to 25 metres, a new tougher liner, modern filtration and the pool surrounds. There will be some extra costs on top: the pavilion will need some work so the pool can reopen with suitable changing and access. <strong>Phase 2</strong> is the full pavilion refurbishment, with new changing rooms, toilets, a reception area and a caf&eacute;. We will fundraise for it separately.</p>
          <p><strong>2028 is our plan, not a promise.</strong> There is still a lot to do, from securing the funding to appointing contractors and building. Opening in 2028 depends on how quickly we can raise the money.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE NEW POOL -->
  <section class="mw-sect tall" style="background: var(--bg-elevated);">
    <div class="mw-wrap">
      <span class="mw-eyebrow">Looking forward</span>
      <h2>Plans for the new pool</h2>
      <div class="pool-plans">
        <div class="pool-plans-text">
          <p>The designs have been shaped by years of consultation with the community and key user groups including local schools, Totnes Sub Aqua Club, Bidwell Brook, Lifeworks and The Brook. Inclusivity, sustainability and the environment are at the heart of everything.</p>
          <p>Our fundraising target for the pool is &pound;1,093,000. Thanks to Section 106 funding, grants and our own fundraising we have made a good start, but there is a long way to go and every contribution matters.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>25-metre swim lanes:</strong>extended from 20 metres to allow proper lengths, with room for up to four lanes</li>
            <li><strong>Warm water:</strong>heated by air source heat pumps powered by solar PV on the pavilion roof, with batteries to maximise the energy generated. <a href="/energy-hub">Read more about our energy systems &rarr;</a></li>
            <li><strong>Extended season:</strong>mid-April into October, with the potential to open all year round</li>
            <li><strong>Improved shallow end:</strong>wide corner steps for families with young children and easier access for everyone</li>
            <li><strong>Full accessible access:</strong>especially important for Bidwell Brook, Lifeworks and The Brook</li>
            <li><strong>Sub-aqua ready:</strong>a thicker liner so Totnes Sub Aqua Club can use their equipment safely</li>
            <li><strong>Modern changing facilities:</strong>non-gendered changing including accessible and family cubicles</li>
            <li><strong>Sustainable build:</strong>excavated earth used to create a Devon bank, UV filtration and automatic dosing to minimise chemical use</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-renders">
          <img src="/images/facilities/pool/renders-of-new-pool/Image1.png.webp" alt="Render of the new Dartington swimming pool" loading="lazy" />
          <img src="/images/facilities/pool/renders-of-new-pool/Image5.png.webp" alt="Render of the new pool pavilion" loading="lazy" />
          <img src="/images/facilities/pool/renders-of-new-pool/Image7.png.webp" alt="New pool render" loading="lazy" />
          <img src="/images/facilities/pool/renders-of-new-pool/Image8.png.webp" alt="New pool render" loading="lazy" />
          <img src="/images/facilities/pool/renders-of-new-pool/Image9.png.webp" alt="New pool render, aerial view" loading="lazy" />
          <img src="/images/facilities/pool/renders-of-new-pool/plan.webp" alt="New pool plan view" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE OLD POOL -->
  <section class="mw-sect">
    <div class="mw-wrap">
      <div class="pool-intro">
        <span class="mw-eyebrow">Our history</span>
        <h2>A pool built by the community, for the community</h2>
        <p class="pool-lead">Dartington Swimming Pool was built by volunteers from the local community over a couple of summers in 1975 and 1976. The playground mounds nearby are partly made from the earth that was excavated to build it.</p>
        <p>Since then it has been a thriving hub, with many local families having generations learn to swim here. It is, in every sense, a pool that has been run by the community for the community.</p>
        <p>Sadly, in September 2022 the liner badly tore and exposed the rotten underlying structure. The pool was unable to open in its current state and has remained closed since. But the community that built this pool has every intention of building it back.</p>
        <p><a href="/documents/Pool-Build-Booklet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read this booklet about the origional build &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="pool-photo-grid">
        <img src="/images/facilities/pool/old-pool/IMG_3157.JPG" alt="The old Dartington swimming pool" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/facilities/pool/old-pool/Photo 02-07-2019, 09 03 55.jpg" alt="Swimming at Dartington" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/facilities/pool/old-pool/287502301_3160188130886595_8149523453936601776_n.jpg" alt="Community swimming at Dartington" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/facilities/pool/old-pool/109802155_626516214633831_5742729953052308489_n.jpg" alt="Dartington pool" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/facilities/pool/old-pool/109808089_367489647565643_2624982532694716731_n.jpg" alt="Dartington pool" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/facilities/pool/old-pool/OLD PHOTOS.jpg" alt="Dartington pool archive" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE JOURNEY -->
  <section class="mw-sect" style="background: var(--bg-elevated);">
    <div class="mw-wrap">
      <span class="mw-eyebrow">Progress</span>
      <h2>The journey so far</h2>
      <p style="max-width: 60ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-7);">In 2020, a small group of volunteers began thinking about what a pool refurbishment could look like. After consulting 235 local households, researching pool standards and working with architects, here is where we have got to and where we are heading.</p>
      <div class="pool-milestones">
        <div class="pool-milestone">
          <span class="pool-milestone-year">2020</span>
          <div class="pool-milestone-body">
            <strong>Volunteers get to work</strong>
            <p>A working party forms, consults 235 households, engages schools and user groups, and commissions <a href="https://www.akirbyarchitects.com">Andrew Kirby Architects</a> for the pre-planning application.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-milestone">
          <span class="pool-milestone-year">Sept 2022</span>
          <div class="pool-milestone-body">
            <strong>Pool closes</strong>
            <p>The liner tears and exposes the rotten structure underneath. The pool closes and the work to rebuild it steps up.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-milestone">
          <span class="pool-milestone-year">Feb 2025</span>
          <div class="pool-milestone-body">
            <strong>Planning permission granted</strong>
            <p>Full planning permission for the new pool, backed by 334 people with no objections.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-milestone">
          <span class="pool-milestone-year">2025</span>
          <div class="pool-milestone-body">
            <strong>Solar panels go up</strong>
            <p>80 solar panels and battery storage are installed on the pavilion roof, ready to heat the new pool. <a href="/energy-hub">Read about the energy hub &rarr;</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-milestone">
          <span class="pool-milestone-year">2026</span>
          <div class="pool-milestone-body">
            <strong>Costed and planned</strong>
            <p>Independent construction cost consultants produce a detailed estimate, and a five-year business plan shows how the pool can run sustainably.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-milestone pool-milestone--now">
          <span class="pool-milestone-year">Autumn 2026</span>
          <div class="pool-milestone-body">
            <strong>Fundraising begins</strong>
            <p>We launch our &pound;1,093,000 fundraising drive, building on money already raised with the help of supporters including the Gibbons Trust, The Normans Family Charity Trust, South West Water and Thrive.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-milestone">
          <span class="pool-milestone-year">2026&ndash;28</span>
          <div class="pool-milestone-body">
            <strong>Raise the funds, appoint the builders</strong>
            <p>Grants, trusts, developer contributions and community fundraising, then tendering and construction.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pool-milestone pool-milestone--next">
          <span class="pool-milestone-year">2028</span>
          <div class="pool-milestone-body">
            <strong>Aiming to reopen</strong>
            <p>Our target for swimming again at Meadowbrook, if the fundraising goes to plan.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GET INVOLVED -->
  <section class="mw-sect">
    <div class="mw-wrap">
      <div class="mw-banner">
        <div>
          <span class="mw-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">Get involved</span>
          <h3>Can you help?</h3>
          <p>This pool was built by volunteers and it will be rebuilt by them too, but we need more hands. We are particularly looking for people with skills in construction and the trades, project management, business planning, fundraising, accountancy, communications and social media. But enthusiasm and time are just as valuable. If you care about this pool, we want to hear from you.</p>
          <p>We hold a weekly pool meeting (in person and on Zoom) and new faces are always welcome. Or if you would prefer a more casual introduction, come and find us at <a href="/events">one of our events</a>.</p>
          <a href="/contact" class="mw-btn mw-btn-ink">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
        <div class="visual" style="background-image: url('/images/facilities/pool/old-pool/IMG_3157.JPG');"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mw-sect tight">
    <div class="mw-wrap">
      <a href="/facilities" class="mw-back">Back to all facilities</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* ---- Latest update ---- */
  .pool-update {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .pool-update > * {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .pool-update-main .pool-lead {
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .pool-target {
    container-type: inline-size;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
  .pool-target-label {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .pool-target-figure {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: min(4.5rem, 10.5cqi);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .pool-target-sub {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .pool-update-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .pool-status {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }
  .pool-status h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .pool-status ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .pool-status li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 2.1rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .pool-status li strong {
    display: block;
  }
  .pool-status li::before {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.05rem;
    width: 1.4rem;
    height: 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .pool-status li.done::before {
    content: "\2713";
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #fff;
  }
  .pool-status li.now::before {
    content: "";
    border: 3px solid var(--accent);
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .pool-status li.next::before {
    content: "";
    border: 2px dashed currentColor;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .pool-detail {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 75ch;
  }
  .pool-detail summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .pool-detail-body p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
  }

  /* ---- Intro ---- */
  .pool-intro {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }
  .pool-intro h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .pool-intro .mw-eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .pool-lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .pool-intro p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* ---- Old pool photo grid ---- */
  .pool-photo-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .pool-photo-grid img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4/3;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    display: block;
  }

  /* ---- Journey section headings ---- */
  section .mw-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  /* ---- Milestones ---- */
  .pool-milestones {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .pool-milestone {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .pool-milestone-year {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .pool-milestone--now .pool-milestone-year {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .pool-milestone--next {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }
  .pool-milestone-body a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .pool-milestone-body strong {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .pool-milestone-body p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    opacity: 0.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ---- New pool plans ---- */
  .pool-plans {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .pool-plans-text p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    max-width: 55ch;
  }
  .pool-plans-text ul {
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .pool-plans-text li {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .pool-plans-text a:not(.mw-btn) {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .pool-renders {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .pool-renders img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4/3;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    display: block;
  }
  .pool-renders img:first-child {
    grid-column: span 2;
    aspect-ratio: 16/9;
  }

  /* ---- Responsive ---- */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .pool-update { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); }
    .pool-photo-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .pool-milestones { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .pool-plans { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .pool-renders img:first-child { aspect-ratio: 4/3; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .pool-photo-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .pool-milestones { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .pool-renders { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .pool-renders img:first-child { grid-column: span 1; }
  }
</style>
